# Per-service Yggdrasil port forwarders

Each `.forward` file defines one socat TCP6→TCP4 forwarder.
Format: shell variables sourced by the entrypoint script.

  PORT=<port to listen on over yggdrasil>
  TARGET=tailscale:<same port>

TARGET is always Caddy, reached as `tailscale:<port>` because Caddy shares the
tailscale container's network namespace. Caddy gets a matching `:<port>` site
block in caddy/conf.d-ygg/. Forwarding straight at a service container instead
would bypass Caddy entirely.

The mesh has no naming, so a service is addressable only as
[<node address>]:<port>, and two services cannot share a port. Ports are
allocated from 9000 up — not from the service's own port, which would let a
service on 80 or 443 collide with Caddy's own listeners.

Example (Jellyfin, listening on 8096 in its container):
  PORT=9000
  TARGET=tailscale:9000

Managed by: homelab ygg enable/disable
